## **4. Rules to follow for the manual-review pipelines**

| Difference                   | Action                                    |
| ---------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Only Elasticsearch hostnames | Ignore                                    |
| Time-travel ingest pipeline  | Ignore for the previously agreed pipeline |
| Environment-specific values  | Retain Non-LMA                            |
| Filter logic changes         | Update from Com-LMA                       |
| Comments or formatting       | Ignore if behaviour is unchanged          |
| New `send_to` routing        | Review and update if required             |
| New processing conditions    | Review and update                         |
| No functional changes        | Leave pipeline unchanged                  |

If a pipeline requires changes, copy its DEV configuration into `updated-dev-pipelines` and update the required sections.

For example:

```
cp -n dev-pipelines/beats-auditbeat.conf \
updated-dev-pipelines/
```

Compare it against PROD:

```
"$VSCODE" --diff \
updated-dev-pipelines/beats-auditbeat.conf \
prod-pipelines/beats-auditbeat.conf
```

